140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (Active vs passive measurement. Active means we send our own test traffic \(ping, traceroute, iperf3\) and measure what happens to it, so we control when and how much, but it adds load. Passive means we just watch real traffic \(Wireshark captures, SNMP counters\) without adding any, so it shows what users really experience, but only for traffic that actually exists.)
/E (Active vs passive measurement. Active means we send our own test traffic \(ping, traceroute, iperf3\) and measure what happens to it, so we control when and how much, but it adds load. Passive means we just watch real traffic \(Wireshark captures, SNMP counters\) without adding any, so it shows what users really experience, but only for traffic that actually exists.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
