709 0 obj
<<
/Title (If the company only measured passively it could still get: link throughput and utilisation \(SNMP interface counters\), real loss and retransmissions, real TCP RTT \(from handshake and ACK timing in captures\), and jitter/loss of real calls from RTP streams. It would miss: the maximum capacity of a path \(nobody tested it\), paths with no traffic right now, one-way delay \(needs synchronised clocks and our own probes\), and any early warning. Problems would be noticed only after users were already hit, which is exactly what happened with the evening complaints. SNMP polled every 5 minutes also averages away short evening bursts. Best approach is a mix: passive all the time, plus a few cheap active probes.)
