<<
/Title (Would 1 Gbps links help? Not much. Transmission drops from 0.12 ms to 0.012 ms per link, so the 4 links go from 0.48 ms to 0.048 ms. New total = 11.848 ms, a saving of only 0.432 ms \(about 3.5%\). A faster link helps big transfers and keeps queues shorter under load, but for a single packet's latency the real fix is a shorter path, meaning a server closer to the student \(CDN or regional server\).)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 853 0 R
/Prev 1011 0 R
>>
endobj
