/Title (An overlay is a virtual network built on top of the normal internet using its own addressing and routing between chosen nodes. A CDN places edge servers in many regions, and DNS or anycast steers each student to the nearest one that caches the content. It would fix frozen recorded video, slow downloads and the load on the origin server, and helps absorb DoS traffic. A VPN builds encrypted tunnels \(IPsec/WireGuard\) between the 20 centres and head office across the internet, so they act like one private network. It fixes secure access and private addressing, but it doesn't improve speed \(it adds overhead\). Neither fixes congestion inside a student's own ISP.)
